%N A220614 Array read by antidiagonals: T(n,k) is the number of ways to reciprocally link elements of an n X k array either to themselves or to exactly two horizontal and vertical neighbors, without consecutive collinear links.
%C A220614 Equivalently, T(n,k) is the number of n X k binary matrices in which every maximal run of 1's in every row and every column has even length (the 1's are the linked elements; each is linked to one horizontal and one vertical neighbor, and the horizontal [vertical] links pair up the 1's of each row [column]). - _Jeff Sponaugle_, Nov 03 2026
